(meta plan
  (id "wiki-review-2026-04")
  (title "CARA wiki design review — correctness remediation")
  (status "active")
  (created "2026-04-17")
  (description "Fix correctness defects from the 2026-04-17 design review of the CARA wiki (zetl static-site output): broken graph links, overlapping graph widget, Sigma runtime errors on small viewports, WCAG-failing chip contrast, broken heading hierarchy from transcluded previews, backlink presentation exposing parser internals, empty tag-cloud page, mobile overflow, search accessibility, and the favicon 404. Design/polish issues from the review (H1 font sizing, visited-link colour, typography, sidebar scaling) are intentionally out of scope."))

;; ── Agents ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
(given agent-claude-available)

;; ── Tasks ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

(given task-graph-page)
(meta task-graph-page
  (description "`_graph.html` 404s on every page in the static build. themes/default/base.html:565 and :637 both href `./_graph.html` (\"Expand ↗\" widget button and sidebar \"Graph\" link). The serve-mode `/_graph` route exists in src/web/mod.rs:410 and the template themes/default/_graph.html exists, but `src/web/build.rs` never renders it to disk. Either emit `_graph.html` during static build (render the existing template against the same graph payload the widget uses) or gate the links to serve mode only.")
  (acceptance "After `zetl build`, opening any generated page and clicking \"Expand ↗\" or sidebar \"Graph\" loads a working graph page (no 404). `curl -sf out/_graph.html` returns 200-equivalent (file exists, parses). Integration test covers presence of `_graph.html` in the static output directory.")
  (priority "P0"))

(given task-widget-overlay)
(meta task-widget-overlay
  (description "Mini-graph widget in base.html:341-357 is `position:fixed; right:16px; bottom:16px; width:400px; height:320px` and is open by default, permanently occluding the last chips of the transclusion-panel and (on help page) body prose. Widget already has a `.zetl-graph-widget__toggle` (base.html:595) and close `×` (base.html:560-563) but no collapsed-default state. Default the widget to collapsed (toggle reveals it); persist last-state in localStorage so returning readers aren't re-prompted.")
  (acceptance "On desktop (≥1025px) a fresh visit shows only the collapsed \"Show graph\" pill in the corner; widget opens when clicked; state persists across navigations. No body content is obscured at 1440px wide on memo-index, togias-2019, help, or landing pages. Existing aria-label on the close button is retained.")
  (priority "P0"))

(given task-widget-zerowidth-guard)
(meta task-widget-zerowidth-guard
  (description "At viewports ≤899px the widget is `display:none` via base.html:487-515, but the Sigma instantiation in themes/default/_graph.html:396 (or the mini-widget's init path) still runs on render tick and throws `Error: Sigma: Container has no width` — reviewer captured 23 instances. Guard instantiation/resize: check `container.offsetWidth > 0` before `new Sigma(...)`, and bail out of resize ticks when width is zero. Related to but narrower than widget-overlay; can ship independently.")
  (acceptance "On a fresh load at 768px and 375px the browser console is free of `Sigma: Container has no width` errors. Resizing from desktop → mobile does not emit repeated errors. Desktop behaviour unchanged.")
  (priority "P0"))

(given task-preview-heading-demotion)
(meta task-preview-heading-demotion
  (description "Reviewer counted 36 `<h1>` elements in the memo-index DOM, breaking the heading outline for screen readers. Root cause: the transclusion preview rendered into `.tc-excerpt` at src/web/build.rs:1023 and src/web/routes.rs:720 embeds the target page's markdown, whose own `# Title` becomes an `<h1>` inside every chip. Demote headings in transclusion previews (h1→h3, h2→h4, etc.) — either strip them in the preview builder or apply a heading-shift pass when rendering excerpts. The chip anchor itself already uses `<a class=\"tc-title\">` (not `<h1>`), so the fix is in the preview body, not the card shell.")
  (acceptance "View-source on memo-index shows exactly one `<h1>` (the page title). Tag-cloud and any page with ≥3 transclusion cards has a linearly valid heading hierarchy (h1 → h2 → h3 with no skipped levels or duplicate h1s). Unit test on the preview builder asserts no h1/h2 survive in rendered excerpt HTML.")
  (priority "P0"))

(given task-chip-contrast)
(meta task-chip-contrast
  (description "All eight chip hues in `.transclusion-panel` (#f472b6 #60a5fa #34d399 #fbbf24 #a78bfa #fb923c #2dd4bf #f87171) fail WCAG 2.1 AA against white — measured contrast 1.67:1 to 2.77:1 vs a 4.5:1 minimum. Chip text colour is applied inline in src/web/build.rs:1022 and src/web/routes.rs:719. Either darken the text palette to AA-compliant variants (e.g. Tailwind *-700 shades), add a subtle filled pill background, or move colour to the left border only and use a single accessible text colour.")
  (acceptance "Every chip title passes WCAG 2.1 AA (≥4.5:1) against its background. A contrast check script or manual audit confirms each of the eight palette entries. Visual regression on togias-2019 / memo-index still shows chips are visually differentiated.")
  (priority "P0"))

(given task-backlinks-presentation)
(meta task-backlinks-presentation
  (description "themes/default/page.html:54 renders every backlink as `line {{ bl.line }}` — raw Markdown line offsets exposed to readers. Also, togias-2019 shows the Memo index twice because it is linked twice from the source (no dedup in src/graph.rs:190-210 backlinks()). Fix both: (a) remove or hide-behind-a-disclosure the `line N` label in the backlinks template, and (b) deduplicate backlink entries by source page — show a single entry, optionally with a `(×N)` count.")
  (acceptance "Viewing any page's Backlinks section shows each source page exactly once; no `line N` suffix appears in the default view. togias-2019 shows Memo index once. Unit test in the graph module asserts dedup by source page.")
  (priority "P1"))

(given task-tag-cloud)
(meta task-tag-cloud
  (description "The advertised `/tag-cloud/` page contains only a placeholder sentence and a raw list of backlinks. There is no tag-cloud route in src/web/routes.rs and no generator in src/web/build.rs. Either (a) build a real tag index from vault frontmatter `tags:` and render counts/links, (b) replace the page body with a clear \"Tag index not yet built\" notice and remove the sidebar link, or (c) drop the page entirely. Preferred: (a) if frontmatter tags are already parsed, otherwise (b).")
  (acceptance "`/tag-cloud/` either shows a real tag listing sourced from vault frontmatter OR a clear placeholder message that does not masquerade as a working feature. Sidebar link matches the page's state (removed if the page is removed).")
  (priority "P1"))

(given task-mobile-overflow)
(meta task-mobile-overflow
  (description "Three related mobile clipping bugs at 375px: (a) long H1 on Lordianto 2018 clips final letter of \"Commissioner\" — add `hyphens:auto; overflow-wrap:anywhere` to `h1` in base.html or step H1 down at narrow breakpoints; (b) help page `<pre>` / code block `cargo install --path . --features \"reason,history,semantic,mcp\"` clips at right edge — add `overflow-x:auto` (and/or `white-space:pre-wrap` for non-code) on `pre` inside `.prose`; (c) landing-page stat-bar shows only 3 of 4 tiles (Orphans clipped) — let the stat grid wrap to 2×2 below ~420px.")
  (acceptance "At 375px: Lordianto H1 renders without truncation; help-page code blocks are horizontally scrollable with no edge clipping; landing stat-bar shows all four tiles (wrapped to 2 rows). Playwright/visual-diff at 375px captures these pages clean.")
  (priority "P1"))

(given task-search-dialog-a11y)
(meta task-search-dialog-a11y
  (description "Search palette at themes/default/base.html:663-668 is a bare `<div class=\"search-dialog\">` with no `role=\"dialog\"`, no `aria-modal=\"true\"`, no `aria-labelledby`, and (per review) no focus trap. Screen reader users are not told a modal opened. Add the ARIA attributes, ensure the input receives focus on open, trap focus within the palette while open, and restore focus to the invoking element on close (Esc).")
  (acceptance "Opening the palette (⌘K) announces a dialog in VoiceOver. Tab/Shift+Tab cycles within the palette. Esc closes and returns focus to the prior element. axe-core or similar a11y scan reports no critical issues on the search modal.")
  (priority "P1"))

(given task-favicon)
(meta task-favicon
  (description "Every page hits `/favicon.ico` and 404s (confirmed in console log). base.html:1-30 has no favicon link. Ship a small favicon (inline SVG or ship a file) and add `<link rel=\"icon\">` to the base template.")
  (acceptance "No `/favicon.ico` 404 in the network log on any generated page. `curl -sf $OUT/favicon.*` returns the expected file or the inline data URL is in the HTML.")
  (priority "P2"))

(given task-search-match-precision)
(meta task-search-match-precision
  (description "Search implementation at base.html:704-745 fuzzy-matches across non-contiguous letters (typing \"hard\" hits both \"hardship\" and \"Pharmacy Depot 2019\" by matching `P**ha**rmacy **D**epot`). As the corpus grows this will confuse users. Prefer a prefix/substring match on title (case-insensitive), optionally falling back to subsequence-fuzzy when nothing matches. Body-text indexing is a larger follow-up and out of scope for this task.")
  (acceptance "Typing \"hard\" matches pages whose title contains the substring \"hard\" (e.g. \"hardship\") and does NOT match \"Pharmacy Depot 2019\". Regression: common queries (\"togias\", \"joint\", \"cara\") still return the expected pages.")
  (priority "P2"))

